            <ArticleTitle>Is niacin ineffective? Or did AIM-HIGH miss its target?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>38-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3949/ccjm.79a.11166</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The AIM-HIGH trial (Atherothrombosis Intervention in Metabolic Syndrome With Low HDL/High Triglycerides: Impact on Global Health Outcomes) found, in an interim analysis, no cardiovascular benefit from taking extended-release niacin (Niaspan). In fact, there was a trend toward a greater risk of ischemic stroke, which did not reach statistical significance. But questions remain about this complex trial, which included intensive statin therapy in the active-treatment group and the control group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
